    "bottomLine": "The two-tool kit to buy if you drive structural screws, drill masonry or work all day, and are happy to commit to Milwaukee M18.",
    "description": "Milwaukee's 2997-22 pairs the 2804-20 M18 FUEL 1/2-inch hammer drill with the 2853-20 M18 FUEL 1/4-inch hex impact driver, both brushless, plus two M18 REDLITHIUM XC5.0 batteries (48-11-1850), an M18 and M12 multi-voltage charger and a carrying case. The drill is listed at 1,200 in-lbs of torque, 0-550/2,000 RPM and 32,000 BPM in hammer mode, with an all-metal ratcheting chuck. The impact driver is rated for 2,000 in-lbs and lists three speeds up to 3,600 RPM and 4,300 IPM. The big batteries are the point of this kit: they carry a long day of deck screws and masonry anchors. Note that this is the earlier FUEL generation. Milwaukee's current FUEL two-tool kit is the 3697-22, but we could not find it listed on Amazon under Milwaukee's own brand, and the 2997-22 is still a very strong pro kit."
  },
  {
    "id": "dewalt-dck277c2",
    "name": "DEWALT 20V MAX Brushless Compact Drill/Driver and Impact Driver Combo Kit (DCK277C2)",
