    "bottomLine": "Big batteries and light, well-balanced tools; the pick for Makita households and anyone who drives screws overhead.",
    "description": "Makita's XT269M combines the XPH12 brushless 1/2-inch hammer driver-drill and the XDT13 brushless impact driver with two BL1840B 4.0Ah batteries, a DC18RC rapid charger and a tool bag. The hammer drill is rated for 530 in-lbs of torque, two speeds of 0-500 and 0-2,000 RPM and up to 30,000 BPM, and Makita lists it at about 4 pounds with a battery. The impact driver is rated for 1,500 in-lbs and is listed at 3.3 pounds with the 4.0Ah pack. That combination of real battery capacity and light tools is what makes the kit. The drill is not a heavy-duty boring tool; for big spade bits and hole saws, the Milwaukee is stronger. For screws, pilot holes, anchors and all-day driving, it is excellent. See our DeWalt vs Makita comparison before committing to the LXT platform."
  },
  {
    "id": "dewalt-dck240c2",
    "name": "DEWALT 20V MAX Drill/Driver and Impact Driver Combo Kit (DCK240C2)",
    "category": "2-Tool Kit, Brushed, 2 x 1.3Ah",
