          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the platform first and the kit second. For most people that means a brushless two-tool kit like the DeWalt DCK277C2, with bigger batteries added when a project calls for them. If you drive structural screws or work all day, the Milwaukee 2997-22 and Makita XT269M earn their price with real battery capacity.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Skip the big kits unless you would have bought the saws anyway, and read the battery suffix on every model number before comparing prices. The cheapest kit is the one whose every part you actually use.
          </p>
